# The native DSP's flat float config: the array Kotlin (NativeBmwDspValues) sends
# configureNativeBmwDsp() and NativeBmwDspProcessor::configure() reads.
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH. After editing, run scripts/gen-dsp-schema.py: it regenerates the C++ header
# (app/src/main/cpp/engine/NativeBmwDspSchema.h), the Kotlin indices and defaults
# (app/src/main/java/app/siphondsp/model/NativeBmwDspSchema.kt), native-tests/default_config.txt and
# docs/NATIVE_BMW_DSP_SCHEMA.md. CI runs it with --check.
#
# Saved tunings are stored by index: slots are append-only. Never move a slot or reuse one for a
# different meaning without a migration; grow the array at the end.
#
#   section <title>
#   slot <n> <default> <reader> <kotlin names|-> <c++ names|-> <description>
#   const <c++ name> <value> <description>          (structure: widths, strides, field offsets)
#
# reader: native   configure() reads and validates it (a non-finite value rejects the update)
#         kotlin   native never reads it: migration marker, UI state, or a legacy value Kotlin
#                  migrates from
#         reserved read by nothing; kept so no later slot moves


section Enabled, retired band passthroughs (1..2), channelMute, measurementMute
slot 0   1           native   INDEX_ENABLED kEnabled enabled
slot 1   0           reserved - - lpfPass (retired: replaced by the crossover bypass, slot 309)
slot 2   0           reserved - - hpfPass (retired: replaced by the crossover bypass, slot 309)
slot 3   0           native   INDEX_CHANNEL_MUTE kChannelMute channelMute
slot 4   0           native   INDEX_MEASUREMENT_MUTE kMeasurementMute measurementMute

